            <ArticleTitle>[Spontaneous emphysema of the mediastinum].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>17-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cases of 104 patients with the spontaneous emphysema of the mediastinum were thoroughly analyzed. The disease affects young men, aged less the 30 years, with asthma or chronic bronchitis. Differentiation should be made between iatrogenic esophageal or tracheobronchial rupture and spontaneous rupture of esophagus. Surgical treatment is indicated to less then 4% of patients with spontaneous mediastinal emphysema.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
